# file and mints a software DOI with this metadata. Update `version` and
# `date-released` before tagging. After the four essays are on Zenodo,
# replace the "PENDING-ESSAY-N" DOIs under `references` with the minted
# concept DOIs and re-tag if needed.

cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below, and
  consider co-citing the accompanying essay series.
title: "Practice Theory: A Working Implementation"
abstract: >-
  A working implementation of the AI-trust-via-practice-theory
  architecture. A substrate of five pools captures the structure of a
  practitioner's situated awareness about a practice (teleo-affective,
  understanding, rules, affordances, materials); projection rules
  assemble a runnable practice from a bundle plus the engagement; an MCP
  server presents the projected practice through a fixed tool surface
  and a practice://* resource surface; an enactment trail records what
  was actually invoked; meta-materials let practices author other
  practices at runtime; an autonomic loop (Judge and Smoother) reads
  the trail and amends the substrate through the same machinery.
  Companion software to the four-essay AI Trust series by the same
  author.
type: software
